{% import "partials/news-cards.njk" as nc %}
{#- Markup taken from design-source/pages/news.html. CONTENT.md marks this
    page's copy "inline (draft)", so the export supplies both; only asset
    references and routes are rewritten. Do not re-author.

    Exception, founder-approved under UNP-82 v1 §4b: Cost Watch is no longer a
    hand-curated reading list of third-party articles. It renders the register's
    own `placement=news-feed` rows, so every entry is a sourced, dated figure
    under the same rule as the rest of the site.

    Exception, founder-approved under N6: the split landing is reversed. /news/
    is now the whole Uncost news page — every update at full length, full
    width — and Cost Watch lives only at /news/cost-watch/. Two half-pages
    served neither; a reader arriving at /news/ wanted the movement's own
    updates, and the ones who wanted prices in the news now get a whole page of
    them instead of a rail. The cross-reference at the top carries them across
    in one line, and the old /news/uncost/ route 301s here (src/_redirects).

    Copy on this page is unchanged: the introband paragraph and the items are
    the approved Uncost-column strings, moved up from the column that is now
    the page. The only new string is the cross-reference line. -#}
<!-- SECTION: news.News — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="News — title"><h1>Uncost.org <span class="u-1">News</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>What&rsquo;s moving &mdash; ours and the world&rsquo;s.</h2>
  <p>What the movement is doing, dated and honest, including the updates that aren&rsquo;t good news.</p>
</div>

<div class="newswrap newswrap--solo">
  <!-- SECTION: news.Updates -->
  <div class="updates" data-screen-label="Updates">
{#- N6 cross-reference. One line at the top of each news route pointing at the
    other, so the two pages stay one section without either having to carry a
    column of the other. -#}
    <div class="newsxref">
      <p>For current cost news from around the web, see <a href="/news/cost-watch/">Cost Watch</a>.</p>
    </div>
{#- N5 keyword filter, same progressive-enhancement pattern as /receipts/: the
    bar ships hidden and only /js/keyword-filter.js reveals it, so with JS off
    every item renders and no dead control is shown. -#}
    <div class="rfilter" data-keyword-filter data-filter-for="news-uncost" data-filter-noun="updates" hidden>
      <label for="ufilter-q">Filter these updates</label>
      <input id="ufilter-q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try &ldquo;policy&rdquo; or &ldquo;repository&rdquo;&hellip;">
      <span class="rfilter-count" data-filter-count></span>
    </div>
    <div id="news-uncost">
{% for item in news %}
      {{ nc.update(item, 3) }}
{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="u-96" id="rss">More updates arrive as the movement launches. Prefer a feed? <a href="/news/feed.xml">Subscribe by RSS</a> &mdash; every update, no algorithm in between.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="/js/keyword-filter.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/read-more.js" defer></script>
